This is an excellent set of UI/UX improvements. Enforcing strict real-time input filtering (preventing bad characters before they are even typed) is a hallmark of a professional, enterprise-grade React application.
Here is a deep analysis of how we will solve each of your requirements:
 1. **Compulsory Common Remarks:** We will unify the validation logic. isRemarksValid will be updated to strictly require 2-30 characters, making both the batch-level and row-level remarks compulsory.
 2. **Strict Space & Character Filtering:** We will update the filterRemarks function to use a chain of Regex replacements. It will strip out non-alphanumerics, strip leading spaces, and collapse multiple consecutive spaces into a single space in real-time.
 3. **Search Constraints (Branch/CGL):** We will create a filterSearchInput function to prevent leading spaces and special characters in the search bar. We will update the API triggers to require a minimum of 3 characters, dynamically update the noOptionsText in the dropdown, and add visual helper text.
